WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.729 --> 00:00:02.889
Let's talk a little bit about Noam Chomsky.

00:00:02.889 --> 00:00:05.700
Noam Chomsky is a linguist and a philosopher.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:13.909
He's now 91 years old and he's had some pretty
damn good takes lately that have unfortunately

00:00:13.909 --> 00:00:17.759
really rattled and shaken up a slice of the
American left wing.

00:00:17.759 --> 00:00:19.580
That's very, very anti.

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:20.800
Joe Biden.

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:26.750
So as an example, a few months ago, maybe
it was a month ago, Noam Chomsky said, of

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:31.460
course, I'm going to vote for Joe Biden and
everybody should vote for Joe Biden.

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:32.980
And that was the take.

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:38.649
And it was not particularly controversial,
but there were a lot of people who were very

00:00:38.649 --> 00:00:43.059
upset with Noam Chomsky, saying that he has
sold out in some way.

00:00:43.059 --> 00:00:48.160
But I was glad to hear him say it, because
there's definitely crossover between Bernie

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:50.239
fans and Chomsky fans.

00:00:50.239 --> 00:00:56.340
And not all of them agree that voting Trump
out to replace him with Biden is good.

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:58.190
Now, I believe that that is good.

00:00:58.190 --> 00:00:59.649
That is the right decision to make.

00:00:59.649 --> 00:01:01.149
So does Noam Chomsky.

00:01:01.149 --> 00:01:06.070
Noam Chomsky was recently interviewed by Michael
Brooks, who has some clips on our channel.

00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:13.170
If you go back in the archives a little bit
and Chomsky said, Trump is undeniably the

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:15.610
worst criminal in history.

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:21.660
And what I like about this is that Chomsky
has shown a commitment not to allow the forest

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:25.540
to be missed for the trees when people start
getting into.

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:32.150
Well, you know, back in the 90s, Biden didn't
take Social Security cuts off the table.

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:35.230
So that means he's running today on cutting
Social Security.

00:01:35.230 --> 00:01:36.320
You know, it's like, hold on.

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:37.320
Hold on a second.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:38.320
Hold on a second.

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:39.320
Up.

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:42.310
Biden is not running on cutting Social Security
today.

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:48.170
In the 90s, Biden said I wouldn't preemptively
take it off the table in a negotiation.

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:53.210
While I disagree with what Biden said in the
90s, that was almost 30 years ago.

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:54.650
And he's not running on that now.

00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:57.490
And Trump is an evil madman who must be removed.

00:01:57.490 --> 00:01:58.490
Noam Chomsky.

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:03.240
It's been very good at distilling that every
time he's asked about this and he does it

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:05.320
here in this interview as well.

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:09.069
Let's look at a sort of condensed transcript
and actually want to read through it, because

00:02:09.069 --> 00:02:10.239
this really matters.

00:02:10.239 --> 00:02:14.060
Noam Chomsky said, quote, This sounds strong,
but it's true.

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:16.299
Trump is the worst criminal in history.

00:02:16.299 --> 00:02:20.640
Undeniably, there has never been a figure
in political history who is so passionately

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:26.790
dedicated to destroying the projects for organized
human life on Earth in the near future.

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:28.390
This is not an exaggeration.

00:02:28.390 --> 00:02:30.280
People are focused now on the protests.

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:35.749
The pandemic is serious enough that we will
emerge from it at a terrible cost.

00:02:35.749 --> 00:02:40.560
The cost is greatly amplified by the gangster
in the White House who has killed tens of

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:45.470
thousands of Americans, making this the worst
place in the world for the corona virus.

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:50.329
We will emerge from the pandemic, but we're
not going to emerge from another crime that

00:02:50.329 --> 00:02:51.680
Trump has committed.

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:54.810
The heating of the globe, the worst of it
is coming.

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:57.150
We're not going to emerge from that.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:02:58.709
The ice sheets are melting.

00:02:58.709 --> 00:03:00.260
They're not going to recover.

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:03.790
That leads to exponential increase in global
warming.

00:03:03.790 --> 00:03:07.310
Arctic glaciers, for example, could flood
the world.

00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:12.390
Recent studies indicate that on the present
course in about 50 years, much of the habitable

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:14.969
part of the world will be unlivable.

00:03:14.969 --> 00:03:18.360
You won't be able to live in parts of South
Asia, parts of the Middle East, parts of the

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:19.819
United States.

00:03:19.819 --> 00:03:24.360
We're approaching the point of one hundred
and twenty five thousand years ago, when sea

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:27.980
levels were about 25 feet higher than they
are now.

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:29.060
And it's worse than that.

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:34.290
The Scripps Oceanographic Institute just came
out with a study that estimated that we are

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:39.840
coming ominously close to a point similar
to three million years ago when sea levels

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:44.349
were 50 to 80 feet higher than they are today.

00:03:44.349 --> 00:03:50.500
Noam Chomsky goes on to say, quote, All around
the world, countries are trying to do something

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:51.500
about it.

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:56.719
But there is one country which is led by a
president who wants to escalate the crisis

00:03:56.719 --> 00:04:02.639
to raced toward the abyss to maximize the
use of fossil fuels, including the most dangerous

00:04:02.639 --> 00:04:07.769
of them, and to dismantle the regulatory apparatus
that limits their impact.

00:04:07.769 --> 00:04:10.299
There is no crime like this in human history.

00:04:10.299 --> 00:04:11.299
Nothing.

00:04:11.299 --> 00:04:15.110
This is a unique individual and it's not as
if he doesn't know what he's doing.

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:16.329
Of course he does.

00:04:16.329 --> 00:04:22.040
It says if he doesn't care if he can pour
more profits into his pockets and the pockets

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:28.570
of his rich constituency tomorrow, who cares
if the world disappears in a couple of generations?

00:04:28.570 --> 00:04:33.890
As far as the government is concerned, we're
seeing something pretty interesting.

00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:38.480
Parliamentary democracy has been around for
350 years, starting in England in sixteen

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:43.690
eighty nine with the so-called glorious revolution
when sovereignty was transferred from the

00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:45.870
royalty to the Parliament.

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:51.290
The beginnings of parliamentary democracy
in the US came about a century later.

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:54.370
Parliamentary democracy is not just based
on laws and constitutions.

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:58.010
In fact, the British Constitution is maybe
a dozen words.

00:04:58.010 --> 00:05:00.630
It's based on trust and good faith.

00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:04.080
The assumption that people will act like human
beings.

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:09.980
And then after Chomsky talks a little bit
about Richard Nixon and George W. Bush.

00:05:09.980 --> 00:05:16.410
Chomsky goes back to quote, It goes deep into
issues well before Trump.

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:18.220
But he is a unique phenomenon.

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:21.660
Again, the worst criminal in human history.

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:28.060
So his minor crimes are to destroy American
democracy and to amplify a pandemic, killing

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:30.340
over a hundred thousand people.

00:05:30.340 --> 00:05:34.640
But those are minor crimes by his standards.

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:42.280
What's so important about this is that Chomsky
distills the importance of not messing around

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:44.890
with these sidebar arguments.

00:05:44.890 --> 00:05:51.500
What we're seeing is as bad as I and others
have been saying, much of it, the incompetence,

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:56.300
the authoritarian tendencies, the ruined global
alliances, the worsening crisis, crisis of

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:59.230
climate change, while Trump doesn't care.

00:05:59.230 --> 00:06:01.840
They were all completely predictable from
day one.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:03.560
And I was not unique in predicting it.

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:06.760
I'm not taking any unique credit for predicting
it.

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:12.010
This is not a time for maybe I'll stay home
or maybe I don't care or I don't really like

00:06:12.010 --> 00:06:17.050
Biden or whatever you contribute to the worsening
of the problem.

00:06:17.050 --> 00:06:20.550
If you do that, that's how critical this is.

00:06:20.550 --> 00:06:24.290
And I'm so glad that we are hearing it from
Noam Chomsky.

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:29.560
We'll have some of these Chomsky quotes on
the show's Instagram page at David Pakman

00:06:29.560 --> 00:06:30.560
show.

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:32.300
Make sure you're following us there.

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:36.460
Also, make sure you're following me on Instagram
at David Pakman.

00:06:36.460 --> 00:06:47.570
I posted a video of how I now drink water.

00:06:47.570 --> 00:07:47.530
Might be interesting to

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:54.470
some of you.

